# Flutter coding style

## Shared string constants

For a small set of related `const` values (e.g. copy shared by UI and services), **prefer top-level `const` in a dedicated library** over a class that only holds `static const` members.

```dart
// ✅ Prefer in e.g. `data/constants/daily_reminder.dart`
const String dailyReminderTitle = '…';
const String dailyReminderSubtitle = '…';

// ❌ Avoid unless you need namespacing at scale or non-const members
class DailyReminderCopy {
  DailyReminderCopy._();
  static const String title = '…';
}
```

Use a **namespace class** when the group grows, you need `static` methods, or disambiguation from other top-level names in the same barrel is painful.

## Naming

Follow project rules: full words, no unnecessary abbreviations; file names must not repeat the folder role (see `no-redundant-filename-suffix`).
